        "rapidmlx/qwen3.8:27b",
        "--title",
        "comparison launch",
        "dump() emits unparseable or lossy output for strings in flow collections when a colon is immediately followed by a flow indicator. For example dump([\":{\"], { flowLevel: 0 }) and dump({ k: \":[\" }, { flowLevel: 0 }) leave the value as a plain scalar, so load(dump(x)) does not give back x for values such as \":{\", \":[\", \":,\", \":}\", \":]\" or \"x:{\". In flow context a colon followed by any of , [ ] { } is not plain-safe (YAML 1.2, ns-plain-safe-in excludes c-flow-indicator), so such values must be quoted when presented in flow style, while block-context output and other plain scalars (for example \"a:b\", or \"x:{\" at block level) must stay exactly as they are today. Source is under src/ (TypeScript); the package is built with npm run build and tests run with node --test \"test/core/**/*.test.mjs\" \"test/spec/*.test.mjs\".\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npm run build && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: node --test test/core/**/*.test.mjs test/spec/*.test.mjs\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/."
      ],
